---
/**
 * Homepage. Two constraints bind the <title> and description below:
 *
 * 1. "Direct-hire" is NOT the business model. In Singapore, "direct hire"
 *    specifically means hiring WITHOUT an agency, which contradicts the
 *    $888 agent fee this same page publishes. Brief §14 lists Direct-Hire
 *    Processing as one of six services, not as what DirectHired is. The
 *    title must say what the business is — a maid agency — and brief §49's
 *    primary search themes lead with "maid agency Singapore" and
 *    "domestic helper agency Singapore". Search intent, not stuffing: each
 *    phrase appears once, inside a sentence a person would actually read.
 *
 * 2. The description is also og:description and the string Google shows in
 *    results. It must not carry a claim this page contradicts: brief §19
 *    permits additional helper placement-related fees, so no completeness
 *    promise ("no hidden markups", "no added fees") belongs here — and an
 *    unevidenced accusation against other agencies least of all.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { employmentAgencySchema } from '../lib/structured-data'
import Hero from '../sections/Hero.astro'
import TrustBar from '../sections/TrustBar.astro'
import Problem from '../sections/Problem.astro'
import Difference from '../sections/Difference.astro'
import Process from '../sections/Process.astro'
import PricingSection from '../sections/PricingSection.astro'
import TwoSidedMatch from '../sections/TwoSidedMatch.astro'
import HelperSources from '../sections/HelperSources.astro'
import Services from '../sections/Services.astro'
import MeetHelpers from '../sections/MeetHelpers.astro'
import Reviews from '../sections/Reviews.astro'
import Faq from '../sections/Faq.astro'
import FinalCta from '../sections/FinalCta.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="DirectHired — Singapore Maid Agency & Domestic Helper Placement"
  description="DirectHired is a Singapore maid agency that understands your household first, then recommends domestic helpers who fit. Clear, itemised package pricing."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(employmentAgencySchema())} slot="head" />
  <Hero />
  <TrustBar />
  <Problem />
  <Difference />
  <Process />
  <PricingSection />
  <TwoSidedMatch />
  <HelperSources />
  <Services />
  <MeetHelpers />
  <Reviews />
  {/*
    <Faq /> with every default, as always. What changed on 2026-08-16 is
    which entries the default `surface="home"` selects, and it changed in
    the CONTENT rather than here: src/content/faq/fly-in-package.md is no
    longer tagged `home`.

    WHY. "What is included in the fly-in package?" answered itself by
    reprinting the six line items — Agent fees, MOM, Insurance, SIP, Medical
    checkup, Handling & transport — and both totals, to a reader who had
    already scrolled past all eight of those figures on the two PricingCards
    in block 06 of this same page. It then closed by restating §2.4's
    advance-and-recover framing in near-identical words to
    PricingSection.astro's qualifier directly under those cards, AND to
    faq/cost.md, which renders immediately above it in this accordion —
    roughly 628 characters apart. One page, one formula, three times.

    THE PRECEDENT IS THIS REPO'S OWN, and it is recorded in
    src/pages/pricing.astro: that page untagged this entry and cost.md for
    exactly this reason, because its cards sit a screen above. The homepage
    carries the same cards. The remedy is the same one, and the reason it is
    UNTAGGING rather than deleting is also the same: neither entry is cut,
    and both still serve /faq, where the reader has not just read the cards.

    NEITHER HALF OF §2.4 IS LOST ANYWHERE. The framing still reaches a
    homepage reader twice — in PricingSection's qualifier under the cards,
    and in cost.md's answer, which is the entry whose question is about
    cost. fly-in-package.md's own closing is unchanged and still carries
    both halves, on /faq. Spec §2.6.4's finding that families re-ask for
    reassurance is not a licence for near-verbatim adjacent repetition;
    that entry says so itself.

    The list is still six long — submit-requirements.md (order 90) moves up
    into the sixth slot — so nothing about this block's height or ground
    rhythm changes.
  */}
  <Faq />
  <FinalCta />
</BaseLayout>
